  "description": "Issue #11 closure POSITIVE runtime proof: boots the debug ROM to the real, live Chapter 4 prep screen (gPlaySt.chapterStateBits PLAY_FLAG_PREPSCREEN=0x10 set by the genuine PrepScreenProc/gProcScr_SALLYCURSOR lifecycle), navigates the on-map prep command menu to 'View Map' so gProcScr_SALLYCURSOR rests in PrepScreenProc_MapIdle, then fires the SELECT+B prep hotkey. DebugTools_PrepHotkeyCheck (called ONLY from PrepScreenProc_MapIdle) increments gDebugToolsProbe.prepScreenObservedCount to 1 because PLAY_FLAG_PREPSCREEN is set, and opens the debug hub (gDebugToolsProbe.hubOpenCount 1->2, sHubActive 0->1). A second SELECT+B proves DebugTools_OpenHub reentrancy/idempotency (hubOpenCount stays 2 -- the sHubActive guard blocks a second StartOrphanMenu) while the same B cleanly cancels the hub menu (sHubActive 1->0), returning to the still-live prep MapIdle (chapterStateBits still 0x10, no crash), and a long-run checkpoint at frame 6000 re-confirms PLAY_FLAG_PREPSCREEN is still set with the hub closed (sHubActive==0). All evidence is relocation-independent semantic EWRAM probes -- PLAY_FLAG_PREPSCREEN, the prep-screen state byte at 0x020210b2, prepScreenObservedCount, hubOpenCount, and sHubActive -- at fixed addresses from this build's own ELF symbol table. The observedCount 0->1 increment (which only DebugTools_PrepHotkeyCheck, itself reachable only from PrepScreenProc_MapIdle, can produce) is itself the proof the hotkey fired from a live MapIdle, so no proc_idleCb/proc_scrCur ROM-pointer oracle is needed or asserted.",
